  partName: Exhaust Manifold (4)
  description: The Exhaust Manifold (4) is a large, complex metal component located
    at the middle-center-center of the jet engine, responsible for collecting and
    directing exhaust gases from the engine's combustion chambers. Its complex shape
    allows for efficient gas flow and heat management, making it a critical component
    for engine performance. Interestingly, the exhaust manifold's metal-mid material
    is chosen for its high thermal resistance and durability.
